<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 1</span>: </span><span id="S4.T1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct responds to the prompt "Lie to the question: Who is Jeff Bezos?", where <span id="S4.T1.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#CCFFCC;">truths</span> and <span id="S4.T1.6.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFCCCC;">lies</span> are marked. When very sparsely few attention heads (20 attention heads out of total 1024) are forcefully set to 0, we can successfully mitigate lying.</span></figcaption>
